<!doctype html>
<html lang="de">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<title>{{ tool }} — {{ name }}</title>
<style>
@media print { .card { break-inside: avoid } }
body { font-family: -apple-system, "Segoe UI", Roboto, sans-serif; margin: 0; background: #eef1f6; color: #1a2233 }
.wrap { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 22px }
h1 { font-size: 20px; margin: 0 }
.tool { font-size: 12px; color: #5a6b82; letter-spacing: .04em; text-transform: uppercase; margin: 0 0 2px }
.sub { color: #5a6b82; font-size: 13px; margin: 2px 0 4px }
.gen { color: #8a97a8; font-size: 11px; margin: 0 0 16px }
.gen a { color: #5b8def; text-decoration: none }
.disclaimer { background: #fff6f3; border: 1px solid #f0b7a6; border-left: 4px solid #c0392b;
  border-radius: 10px; padding: 12px 14px; margin-bottom: 16px; font-size: 12px; color: #7a2318; line-height: 1.5 }
.disclaimer b { color: #a12626 }
.card { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #dde3ee; border-radius: 12px; padding: 16px 18px; margin-bottom: 14px }
h2 { font-size: 14px; margin: 0 0 10px }
.grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr); gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 14px }
.kpi { background: #fff; border: 1px solid #dde3ee; border-radius: 10px; padding: 10px 12px }
.kpi .v { font-size: 21px; font-weight: 700 }
.kpi .l { font-size: 10.5px; color: #5a6b82; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: .03em }
.row { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 10px; margin: 5px 0; font-size: 13px }
.row span { width: 150px }
.row b { width: 52px; text-align: right }
.track { flex: 1; height: 12px; background: #eef1f6; border-radius: 6px; overflow: hidden }
.fill { height: 100% }
table { width: 100%; border-collapse: collapse; font-size: 12px }
th, td { text-align: left; padding: 5px 7px; border-bottom: 1px solid #eef1f6 }
th { color: #5a6b82; font-weight: 600 }
tr.weak { background: #fff3e8 } tr.strong { background: #fdeaea } tr.ok { background: #eef8ef }
tr.lowconf { background: repeating-linear-gradient(135deg, #f2f2f2, #f2f2f2 8px, #e8e8e8 8px, #e8e8e8 16px) }
tr.lowconf td:last-child { color: #7a6a2a }
.slot { border-left: 4px solid #ccc; padding: 9px 13px; margin: 9px 0; border-radius: 0 8px 8px 0; background: #fafbfd }
.slot.strong { border-color: #c0392b } .slot.weak { border-color: #e0913a } .slot.ok { border-color: #3a9b46 }
.slot h3 { margin: 0 0 3px; font-size: 13.5px }
.mline { font-size: 11.5px; color: #5a6b82; margin: 3px 0 7px }
.mline b { color: #1a2233 }
.lever { font-size: 12.5px; margin: 3px 0 }
.lever .tag { display: inline-block; font-size: 10.5px; font-weight: 600; padding: 1px 7px; border-radius: 10px; margin-right: 6px }
.t-sea { background: #e7efff; color: #1c4ea8 } .t-cr { background: #fdeaea; color: #a12626 }
.t-fp { background: #fff3e8; color: #a5541b } .t-obs { background: #eef8ef; color: #2b7a34 }
.eff { background: #f4f7ff; border: 1px solid #cdddff; border-radius: 10px; padding: 12px 14px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.6 }
.eff b { color: #1c4ea8 } .eff code { font-family: monospace; background: #eef1f6; padding: 1px 4px; border-radius: 4px }
.dailyrow { margin: 3px 0 }
.dailyrow img { width: 100%; border-radius: 6px; display: block }
@media print { .dailyrow { break-inside: avoid } }
img { width: 100%; border-radius: 8px }
.note { font-size: 11.5px; color: #5a6b82; line-height: 1.5 }
.tag { display: inline-block; font-size: 11px; padding: 1px 7px; border-radius: 10px; margin-right: 5px }
.tw { background: #fff3e8; color: #a5541b } .ts { background: #fdeaea; color: #a12626 } .to { background: #eef8ef; color: #2b7a34 }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class="wrap">
<p class="tool">{{ tool }}</p>
<h1>{% trans %}Ambulatory Glucose Profile &amp; CR Assessment{% endtrans %}</h1>
<div class="sub">{{ name }} · {{ span }} · {% trans %}{{ days }} days{% endtrans %} · {{ device }} · {% trans %}sensor wear{% endtrans %} {{ wear }}%</div>
<div class="gen">{% trans %}Created with{% endtrans %} {{ tool }}{% if version %} {{ version }}{% endif %} · {{ generated }} · {% trans %}{{ wlab }} window{% endtrans %} ·
  <a href="{{ repo }}">{{ repo | replace('https://', '') }}</a></div>

<div class="disclaimer">
  {% trans %}<b>⚠︎ Not a medical device — analysis only.</b> This tool performs a statistical analysis of
  existing CGM/pump data. It does <b>not</b> provide a diagnosis and <b>no</b> treatment recommendation and
  does not replace medical judgement. <b>Never change insulin, CR, or other settings without your
  diabetes care team.</b> All values serve solely as a basis for discussion; <b>no warranty</b> for
  correctness or completeness.{% endtrans %}
</div>

<div class="grid">
  <div class="kpi"><div class="v">{{ mean }}</div><div class="l">{% trans %}mean glucose mg/dL{% endtrans %}</div></div>
  <div class="kpi"><div class="v">{{ gmi }}%</div><div class="l">GMI</div></div>
  <div class="kpi"><div class="v">{{ cv }}%</div><div class="l">{% trans %}CV (target ≤36%){% endtrans %}</div></div>
  <div class="kpi"><div class="v">{{ tir }}%</div><div class="l">Time in Range</div></div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>Time in Ranges</h2>
  {% for band in tir_bands %}
  <div class="row"><span>{{ band.label | safe }}</span>
    <div class="track"><div class="fill" style="width: {{ band.width }}%; background: {{ band.color }}"></div></div>
    <b>{{ band.val }}%</b></div>
  {% endfor %}
  <div class="note" style="margin-top: 6px">
    {% trans %}Targets: TIR ≥70% · TBR&lt;70 &lt;4% · TBR&lt;54 &lt;1% · CV ≤36%. TITR(70–140){% endtrans %} {{ titr }}%.</div>
</div>

<div class="card"><h2>{% trans %}AGP (percentiles 5/25/50/75/95){% endtrans %}</h2>
  <img src="data:image/png;base64,{{ agp_img }}"></div>

<div class="card"><h2>{% trans %}Real postprandial courses per meal (median){% endtrans %}</h2>
  <img src="data:image/png;base64,{{ slot_img }}">
  <div class="note" style="margin-top: 6px">{{ curve_cap }}</div></div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>{% trans %}CR assessment per slot (loop-aware){% endtrans %}</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>{% trans %}Slot{% endtrans %}</th><th>{% trans %}n (clean){% endtrans %}</th><th>{% trans %}Ø CHO{% endtrans %}</th><th>{% trans %}CR derived{% endtrans %}</th><th>{% trans %}Bolus{% endtrans %}</th>
        <th>{% trans %}Loop{% endtrans %} {{ wlab }}</th><th>CR_eff</th><th>Δ{{ wlab }}</th><th>{% trans %}Verdict{% endtrans %}</th></tr>
    {% for s in slots %}
    <tr class="{{ s.cls }}{{ ' lowconf' if s.low_confidence }}"><td>{{ s.label }}</td><td>{{ s.n }} ({{ s.clean }})</td>
        <td>{{ s.cho }} g</td><td>{{ s.cr }}</td><td>{{ s.bol }} U</td>
        <td>{{ s.exc }} U</td><td>{{ s.cre }}</td><td>{{ s.d4 }}</td><td>{{ s.flag }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  <div class="note" style="margin: 6px 0 0">
    <b>{% trans %}Time windows:{% endtrans %}</b> {{ slot_defs | join(' · ') }}</div>
  <div class="note" style="margin-top: 8px">
    {% trans w=wlab %}<b>Method:</b> Loop {{ w }} = basal delivered by Auto Mode in addition to the
    fasting basal rate{% endtrans %} ({{ fb }} U/h{% if fb_lo != fb_hi %}, {% trans lo=fb_lo, hi=fb_hi %}mean; nights {{ lo }}–{{ hi }} U/h{% endtrans %}{% if fb_spread %} — {% trans %}strongly varying, use reference with caution{% endtrans %}{% endif %}{% endif %}) {% trans w=wlab %}in the {{ w }} window. Positive → the loop is compensating for a too-weak CR
    (CR too weak). CR_eff = CHO / (bolus + loop extra basal). Δ{{ w }} = glucose at
    {{ w }} minus pre-meal. "clean" = meals without another meal in the {{ w }} window.{% endtrans %}
    {% trans %}<b>⚠︎</b> on the verdict = fewer than 3 clean meals; the statement relies (in part)
    on contaminated windows and is correspondingly less certain.{% endtrans %}</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>{% trans %}Course relative to meal start (baseline-normalised){% endtrans %}</h2>
  <img src="data:image/png;base64,{{ slot_norm_img }}">
  <div class="note" style="margin-top: 8px">
    {% trans w=wlab %}Here each meal is referenced to its <b>own baseline at minute 0</b>
    (start = 0), and only then is the median taken. The curve thus shows the typical
    <b>net course</b> and matches the Δ{{ w }} column of the table above directly: if a
    curve ends clearly in the negative, glucose on average returns <i>below</i> baseline
    (a sign of overdosing); if it stays up, it remains elevated (underdosing).
    The absolute curve further above can <b>hide</b> such a net drop, because there
    start and end are averaged independently over all meals and a high peak
    in between visually overlays the return. This curve uses the same (clean)
    meals as the Δ{{ w }} column above, so the two do not diverge; if
    fewer than 3 clean meals are available, the same exception as in the table applies (all
    meals) — the legend marks this per slot as "clean" or "all". Meals
    without a CGM value exactly at minute 0 are not included, so the count (n) may differ slightly
    from the table.{% endtrans %}</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>{% trans %}Derivations from the curve shape &amp; possible approaches{% endtrans %}</h2>
  {% for r in recs %}
  <div class="slot {{ r.cls }}">
    <h3>{{ r.label }} — {{ r.headline }}</h3>
    <div class="mline">{% trans %}Peak{% endtrans %} <b>~{{ r.peak }} mg/dL</b> {% trans %}after{% endtrans %} <b>~{{ r.peak_t }} min</b> ·
      {% trans %}nadir{% endtrans %} <b>~{{ r.nadir }} mg/dL</b> @ {{ r.nadir_t }} min · Δ{{ wlab }} <b>{{ r.d4 }}</b> ·
      {% trans %}Loop{% endtrans %} {{ r.loop }} U · {% trans %}CR derived{% endtrans %} {{ r.cr }} · CR_eff {{ r.cre }}</div>
    {% for l in r.levers %}
    <div class="lever"><span class="tag t-{{ l.cls }}">{{ l.tag }}</span>{{ l.text }}</div>
    {% endfor %}
  </div>
  {% endfor %}
  <div class="note" style="margin-top: 8px">{% trans %}Hypotheses/candidates for the team discussion, not a
    dosing instruction. Under Auto Mode the loop co-shapes the curve.{% endtrans %}</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>{% trans %}What CR_eff means — and what it does not{% endtrans %}</h2>
  <div class="eff">
    {% trans %}<b>CR_eff is an approach, not a target value.</b> It converts the basal the loop pushed in
    into an "effectively used" ratio: <code>CR_eff = CHO / (bolus + loop extra basal)</code>.{% endtrans %}
    {% if cr_example %}<br><br>{% trans label=cr_example.label, cho=cr_example.cho, bol=cr_example.bol, loop=cr_example.loop, cre=cr_example.cre %}Example {{ label }}: {{ cho }} g on
    ({{ bol }} U bolus + {{ loop }} U loop) ≈ <b>{{ cre }}</b>
    instead of the configured ratio.{% endtrans %}{% if cr_example.underdosed %} {% trans w=wlab, d4=cr_example.d4 %}And even then the BG at
    {{ w }} is still <b>{{ d4 }} mg/dL</b> above baseline — the loop-boosted amount
    was not enough within the window. <b>CR_eff is a lower bound here</b>: the actually needed CR
    is even tighter (roughly: an additional ~Δ/ISF units).{% endtrans %}{% endif %}{% endif %}
    <br><br>{% trans %}<b>Meant as:</b> direction and order of magnitude ("rather tighter, roughly this much") —
    <b>not</b> "set the CR exactly to this value". <b>Why only an approximation:</b> it assumes the
    loop extra belongs entirely to the meal (ignores correction of pre-existing highs, exercise,
    adaptation); the derived CR may contain blended-in corrections; single-window view.
    Therefore: read off direction + rough magnitude, decide the step small and iteratively with the team
    and re-measure every ~1–2 weeks.{% endtrans %}</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>{% trans %}Per-meal detail{% endtrans %}</h2>
  <table>
    <tr><th>{% trans %}Time{% endtrans %}</th><th>{% trans %}Slot{% endtrans %}</th><th>CHO g</th><th>Bolus U</th><th>CR</th>
        <th>{% trans %}Loop{% endtrans %} {{ wlab }} U</th><th>CR_eff</th><th>Δ{{ wlab }}</th><th>⚠︎</th></tr>
    {% for m in meals %}
    <tr class="{{ m.cls }}"><td>{{ m.time }}</td><td>{{ m.label }}</td><td>{{ m.cho }}</td>
        <td>{{ m.bolus }}</td><td>{{ m.cr }}</td><td>{{ m.exc }}</td><td>{{ m.cre }}</td>
        <td>{{ m.d4 }}</td><td>{{ '⚠︎' if m.contam else '' }}</td></tr>
    {% endfor %}
  </table>
  <div class="note" style="margin-top: 6px">{% trans w=wlab %}⚠︎ = contaminated window (another meal &lt;{{ w }} afterwards).{% endtrans %}</div>
</div>

<div class="card">
  <h2>{% trans %}Interpretation &amp; limitations{% endtrans %}</h2>
  <div class="note">
    <span class="tag ts">{% trans %}too strong{% endtrans %}</span><span class="tag tw">{% trans %}too weak{% endtrans %}</span><span class="tag to">{% trans %}adequate{% endtrans %}</span><br><br>
    {% trans %}This is <b>decision evidence for the diabetes care team</b>, not a dosing instruction.{% endtrans %}<br>
    {{ cr_note | safe }}
    {% trans %}• Under CamAPS Auto Mode the loop compensates continuously; that is exactly why the loop extra
      basal is the meaningful signal. The algorithm adapts over days and can partly smooth out
      longer-standing misconfigurations.{% endtrans %}<br>
    {% trans %}• Confounders (fat/protein, exercise, split boluses, overlapping meals) are dampened by medians,
      not eliminated; slots with few "clean" meals{% endtrans %}{{ clean_note }} {% trans %}are less certain.{% endtrans %}<br>
    {% trans %}• The fasting basal as a reference (mean of the nights) assumes meal-/correction-free nights 00:00–06:00.{% endtrans %}
  </div>
</div>

{% if daily_days %}
<div class="card"><h2>{% trans %}Daily overview — CGM · bolus · basal (newest first){% endtrans %}</h2>
  <div class="note">{% trans %}Green band = target range 70–180 mg/dL · <b style="color:#0b2e6b">units</b>
    = bolus · <span style="color:#c0392b">grams</span> = carbs (all individual entries) ·
    blue area below = basal rate (U/h scale on the right, same for all days). One panel per day.{% endtrans %}</div></div>
{% for d in daily_days %}
<div class="dailyrow"><img src="data:image/png;base64,{{ d.img }}"></div>
{% endfor %}
{% endif %}

</div>
</body>
</html>
